        "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-011.function-body/text": {
          "file": "locales/en-US/OCF-BOD-011-Hormonal-Transitions.yaml",
          "value": "From this moment forward, your body's natural\nprocesses of hormonal regulation are becoming\nsmoother, more balanced, and more harmonious.\n\nYour body recognizes its changing needs\nand adjusts naturally and appropriately\nthrough every stage of life.\n\nYour hormonal systems work together\nin harmony, maintaining the balance\nneeded for your physical and emotional\nwell-being.\n\nAs your hormone levels naturally change,\nyour body adapts smoothly and efficiently,\nmaintaining its strength, comfort, and stability.\n\nUnnecessary physical discomfort and tension\nwill diminish, allowing your body\nto remain comfortable and at ease.\n\nYour emotions will become calm and steady,\nyour thoughts clear and focused,\nand your sense of inner balance stronger.\n\nYou will move through hormonal changes\nwith greater comfort, confidence,\nand emotional stability.\n\nFrom this moment forward, this pattern\nof healthy regulation and adaptation\nis firmly and permanently established within you.\n\nWhether awake, resting, or sleeping,\nyour body's natural regulatory systems\ncontinue working automatically,\nmaintaining the balance appropriate\nfor your changing needs.\n\nWhenever you wish to reinforce this\npattern of hormonal balance and harmony,\ninhale deeply and gently hold your breath.\n\nThink or say in your mind,\n\"{{ cue.primary }}.\"\n\nThen exhale slowly through your mouth,\nas though gently blowing out a candle.\n\nYour body will return to its natural balance,\neasing unwanted physical, mental,\nand emotional effects of hormonal changes.\n\nEach time you use {{ cue.primary }},\nthis process becomes easier, smoother,\nand more effective.\n\nYour natural pattern of hormonal regulation,\ncomfort, and harmony will continue\nworking automatically,\nevery day and every night.",
          "yaml_pointer": "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-011.function-body/text"
        },
